plugin-qualify (0.8.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Accept omx-contract 2.11: the measurer reads only the declared rates, so
    the floor stays 2.10.1 and the ceiling is < 2.12 (omx-dsp#97)
  * The leak check ignores liblilv's own world leak
  * The leak check covers the plugin-not-found exit too (#40)
  * README: say what the npm package does not ship
  * The ASan build of lv2_measure reads omx-contract's header too (#40)
  * README: the npm package exists, say how to install it (#38)
  * Leave the version at 0.7.0; the release PR sets 0.8.0
  * omx-contract range is one minor wide: >= 2.10.1, < 2.11
  * lv2-measure reads its rates from omx-contract's limits header (#50)
  * qualify: an auxiliary input refuses the CLAP plugin
  * Version 0.9.0 (#40)
  * A leak check runs lv2_measure under AddressSanitizer on every way out
    (#40)
  * lv2_measure frees the host, and what it read of the plugin, on every way
    out (#40)
  * Test the prober reads a name holding a comma or a space as unpinnable
    (#28)
  * Test readIntegrity's refusals: '..', '.', an empty segment, a leading
    '/', a path twice, no files (#28)
  * Version 0.8.0 (#31)
  * Take a native tool and its interposer from one place, and refuse a place
    holding only one (#31)
  * Look for the native tools in the checkout's own build before the
    installed directories (#31)
  * README: install from the npm registry

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:27:53 +0000
